"003:001 And Joram the son of Achaab began to reign in Israel in the eighteenth year of Josaphat king of Juda, and he reigned twelve years.",
"003:002 And he did that which was evil in the sight of the Lord, only not as his father, nor as his mother: and he removed the pillars of Baal which his father had made.",
"003:003 Only he adhered to the sin of Jeroboam the son of Nabat, who made Israel to sin; he departed not from it.",
"003:004 And Mosa king of Moab was a sheep-master, and he rendered to the king of Israel in the beginning of the year, one hundred thousand lambs, and one hundred thousand rams, with the wool.",
"003:005 And it came to pass, after the death of Achaab, that the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel.",
"003:006 And king Joram went forth in that day out of Samaria, and numbered Israel.",
"003:007 And he went and sent to Josaphat king of Juda, saying, The king of Moab has rebelled against me: will you go with me against Moab to war? And he said, I will go up: you are as I, I am as you; as my people, so is your people, as my horses, so are your horses.",
"003:008 And he said, What way shall I go up? and he said, The way of the wilderness of Edom.",
"003:009 And the king of Israel went, and the king of Juda, and the king of Edom: and they fetched a compass of seven days' journey; and there was no water for the army, and for the cattle that went with them.",
"003:010 And the king of Israel said, Alas! that the Lord should have called the three kings on their way, to give them into the hand of Moab.",
"003:011 And Josaphat said, Is there not here a prophet of the Lord, that we may enquire of the Lord by him? And one of the servants of the king of Israel answered and said, There is here Elisaie son of Saphat, who poured water on the hands of Eliu.",
"003:012 And Josaphat said, He has the word of the Lord. And the king of Israel, and Josaphat king of Juda, and the king of Edom, went down to him.",
"003:013 And Elisaie said to the king of Israel, What have I to do with you? go to the prophets of your father, and the prophets of your mother. And the king of Israel said to him, Has the Lord called the three kings to deliver them into the hands of Moab?",
"003:014 And Elisaie said, As the Lord of hosts before whom I stand lives, unless I regarded the presence of Josaphat the king of Juda, I would not have looked on you, nor seen you.",
"003:015 And now fetch me a harper. And it came to pass, as the harper harped, that the hand of the Lord came upon him.",
"003:016 And he said, Thus says the Lord, Make this valley full of trenches.",
"003:017 For thus says the Lord, You shall not see wind, neither shall you see rain, yet this valley shall be filled with water, and you, and your flocks, and your cattle shall drink.",
"003:018 And this is a light thing in the eyes of the Lord: I will also deliver Moab into your hand.",
"003:019 And you shall strike every strong city, and you shall cut down every good tree, and you shall stop all wells of water, and spoil every good piece of land with stones.",
"003:020 And it came to pass in the morning, when the sacrifice was offered, that, behold! waters came from the way of Edom, and the land was filled with water.",
"003:021 And all Moab heard that the three kings were come up to fight against them; and they cried out on every side, even all that were girded with a girdle, and they said, Ho! and stood upon the border.",
"003:022 And they rose early in the morning, and the sun rose upon the waters, and Moab saw the waters on the opposite side red as blood.",
"003:023 And they said, This is the blood of the sword; and the kings have fought, and each man has struck his neighbour; now then to the spoils, Moab.",
"003:024 And they entered into the camp of Israel; and Israel arose and struck Moab, and they fled from before them; and they went on and struck Moab as they went.",
"003:025 And they razed the cities, and cast every man his stone on every good piece of land and filled it; and they stopped every well, and cut down every good tree, until they left only the stones of the wall cast down; and the slingers compassed the land, and struck it.",
"003:026 And the king of Moab saw that the battle prevailed against him; and he took with him seven hundred men that drew sword, to cut through to the king of Edom: and they could not.",
"003:027 And he took his oldest son whom he had designed to reign in his stead, and offered him up for a whole burnt offering on the walls. And there was a great indignation against Israel; and they departed from him, and returned to their land."
